__pycache__/
*.pyc

# AGS/TS typecheck artifacts. `ags types -u` regenerates all of these from the
# GTK/Astal libraries installed on THIS machine: @girs/ is 168 .d.ts files and
# ~49 MB, and node_modules/ holds symlinks into /usr/share/ags/js. They describe
# the local toolchain, not the repo, so they are rebuilt on demand via
# `make capture-types` and never committed. node_modules must never be deployed
# — placement is per-file (gui_tools_app_files), so an unregistered directory
# simply never ships, but it also must never reach a commit.
/src/gui-tools/capture-tool/@girs/
/src/gui-tools/capture-tool/node_modules/
/src/gui-tools/capture-tool/tsconfig.json
/src/gui-tools/capture-tool/env.d.ts
# Bar typecheck (bar-typecheck): the bar tree reuses the capture tool's
# generated @girs/env.d.ts rather than generating its own 49 MB copy, so the
# only generated artifact here is node_modules/ (same symlinks into
# /usr/share/ags/js). tsconfig.json is listed for the same reason as the
# capture one: `ags types` writes its OWN tsconfig.json into whichever
# directory it runs against, and the committed config deliberately uses a
# non-colliding name so it survives.
/dotfiles/config/ags/node_modules/
/dotfiles/config/ags/tsconfig.json
# TypeScript itself, installed with `npm install --no-save typescript` so that
# `npx tsc` resolves from the tool directory without a package.json.
/node_modules/
# The dev-time ags-platform checkout `make ags-platform-dev` fetches on demand
# (pinned, shallow, anonymous). It is the target of the dev
# `dotfiles/config/ags/node_modules/ags-platform` shortcut. Deliberately OUTSIDE
# node_modules: Node refuses to type-strip `.ts` under a real node_modules dir,
# but realpaths a symlink, so the checkout must live here. A committed copy of
# the consumed unit would defeat AD-17 (consume the published unit, not a
# vendored one).
/.dev/
# @types/node, for the domain unit tests' node:test / node:assert. `make
# capture-test` installs it HERE, on demand, under tests/ and nowhere else (see
# the capture-test-deps target). The location is load-bearing in two independent
# ways, both measured: (a) tsconfig.capture.json pins "types": [], so the GJS
# app's ambient surface is empty by intent; (b) tests/ is BELOW the app config's
# own directory, so the default typeRoots walk never descends into it even if
# that pin were deleted. Relocate it to the repo root or to capture-tool/ and
# the walk reaches it — measured at 66 @types/node files joining the app
# program. The path is ignored explicitly because the capture tool's placement
# is per-file and a committed node_modules is a deployment hazard.
/src/gui-tools/capture-tool/tests/node_modules/
# @types/node, for the AGS config's pure-module unit tests (node:test /
# node:assert). `make ags-test` installs it HERE, on demand, beside
# tests/tsconfig.tests.json and nowhere else (see the ags-test-deps target), for
# the same reason as the capture tool's copy above: it must be where tsc's
# upward typeRoots walk finds it and NOT where any future app tsconfig's walk
# would, and a committed node_modules is a deployment hazard.
#
# The trailing `/**/node_modules/` — not the single path above — is what keeps
# the rule true. An install run with the wrong --prefix landed 123 files at
# tests/ts/node_modules/ instead, and a single-path rule let them sit
# untracked-but-committable: `git add -A` would have swept them in, because
# being ignored is the only thing standing between an on-demand install and the
# commit. `git add -An | grep -c node_modules` must stay 0.
/dotfiles/config/ags/tests/node_modules/
/dotfiles/config/ags/tests/**/node_modules/
/package-lock.json
/package.json
/src/cli-tools/wallpaper-effects-generator/feedback.md
/src/cli-tools/wallpaper-effects-generator/test.sh

# Dev VM runtime artifacts (downloaded image, working disk, SSH key, seed)
/dev/.images/

# CSG determinism verification artifact — machine-specific (timestamp, host template hash, podman state)
# Written by src/runtime/tests/integration/test_csg_determinism.py atomically; not for version control
/src/runtime/tests/integration/.csg_determinism.json

# Worktrees live INSIDE the repo, never as sibling dirs. `scripts/worktree-guard.sh
# create <id> <slug>` makes `.worktrees/<id>/` on branch `ticket/<id>-<slug>` so
# every piece of work sits on a branch off master and main stays untouched. The
# guard aborts if master is dirty. Ignored so worktrees never reach a commit.
/.worktrees/
